 Register field values this testbench constrains, loaded after the framework's
 own register_field_choices_rv64.xml.

 mstatus.WPRI covers bits 36-62 and 23-31 on RV64, and FORCE randomises it like
 any other field, and its boot code writes the result. On this core bit 37 is
 not reserved: it is mstatus.MBE, and CVA6 implements it. mbe reaches the
 load and store units, which byte-reverse per access size. The reference is
 built little-endian and holds the bit at zero. Both are conformant, because MBE
 is WARL and an implementation may provide one endianness or both, but once the
 bit is set the two disagree about the meaning of every load and store in the
 program.

 Writing zeros to a WPRI span is what software is supposed to do in any case.
-->
<choices_file>
  <choices name="mstatus.WPRI" type="RegisterFieldValue">
    <choice description="Reserved fields written as zero" value="0x0" weight="100"/>
  </choices>
  <choices name="sstatus.WPRI" type="RegisterFieldValue">
    <choice description="Reserved fields written as zero" value="0x0" weight="100"/>
  </choices>
</choices_file>
